.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rosregview-tree 1  "rosregview-tree "
.SH NAME
rosregview\-tree \- Recursively print the key tree of a hive file (uses ASCII\-only indent)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrosregview tree\fR [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-depth\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Recursively print the key tree of a hive file (uses ASCII\-only indent)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-depth\fR \fI<N>\fR
Maximum recursion depth. 0 = show only the root, 1 = root + direct children, 2 = up to grand\-children, ... Default: unlimited
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]
Output format (`human` is the indented text tree, `json` is machine\-readable)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Path to a .hiv file (Windows registry configuration unit)
